{
  "schema": "ora.toolkit-tool.v1",
  "name": "grasp_plan",
  "description": "Generate inspectable public RGB-D grasp candidates for one current target.\nUse when: current grounding or segmentation identifies the intended object and you need parallel-jaw poses. Select the arm that will grasp.\nEffect: read-only; queries Contact-GraspNet using the selected source-camera RGB-D fused with the overhead camera and the selected arm's wrist camera, and compiles poses to that arm's public TCP (the centre of the two fingertip facets, local z the approach and local x the closing line). Optional synchronized views provide review evidence.\nReturns: up to three candidates, complete world-frame pregrasp_pose and contact_pose, copyable bounded contact_approach targets, predicted opening, compiler checks and labeled review images. Reachability is not checked here: move_pose plans and admits every motion itself. Inspect every candidate panel and choose target identity and geometry independently of rank. Command the selected pregrasp_pose with move_pose, open the gripper with set_gripper if it is not open, approach with the candidate's approach_delta, then close with set_gripper; read each receipt and the fresh observation before the next step. Re-plan candidates after any world action. Pose handoff: when commanding a returned world pose, set position_mode=absolute and orientation_mode=absolute_quaternion, then copy position_m and orientation_xyzw unchanged. Put these fields under targets.<selected_arm>. Choose interaction by the intended physical contact. Schema example only; replace the illustrative pose and arm with your selected current result:\n{\"tool\":\"move_pose\",\"arguments\":{\"targets\":{\"right\":{\"position_mode\":\"absolute\",\"position_m\":[0.35,-0.1,0.12],\"orientation_mode\":\"absolute_quaternion\",\"orientation_xyzw\":[1.0,0.0,0.0,0.0],\"interaction\":\"precision\"}}}}\nDoes not: plan trajectories, certify reachability, move the robot, command a gripper, use object ground truth, certify retention or report task success. Backend rank is not a success probability. Missing optional review cameras do not invalidate usable primary input.\nOn error: Refused: a target_ref unknown in this round (target_ref_unavailable) or bound to an earlier observation (stale_observation); max_candidates outside 1 to 3; an arm outside this tool's enum; unusable primary RGB-D, an uncalibrated camera or a transient backend failure (grasp_proposal_failed); a request the grasp-proposal service rejects (invalid_arguments, with the service's detail). Not refused but moved to diagnostics.rejected: a candidate whose predicted opening exceeds the 93.9 mm nominal ceiling, or whose controlled point or pregrasp lies outside the action workspace; with none left the result is status no_candidate. Obtain a better current view or select another target or candidate. Recompute after the target or observation changes. After a submitted motion fails, use its failure_code and measured pose error to choose the next action.",
  "inputSchema": {
    "type": "object",
    "properties": {
      "arm": {
        "type": "string",
        "enum": [
          "left",
          "right"
        ],
        "description": "Arm that will grasp: its wrist RGB-D joins overhead in scene fusion and the candidates are compiled to its TCP."
      },
      "target_ref": {
        "type": "string",
        "pattern": "^target-[0-9a-f]{24}$",
        "description": "Current observation-bound target from grounding or segmentation; target-mask points remain tied to its source camera."
      },
      "max_candidates": {
        "type": [
          "integer",
          "null"
        ],
        "minimum": 1,
        "maximum": 3,
        "default": 3,
        "description": "Maximum candidates returned, 1 to 3, default 3, in backend order; it does not select a grasp. Null means omitted."
      }
    },
    "required": [
      "arm",
      "target_ref"
    ],
    "additionalProperties": false
  },
